One main package holding a dead component of three declarations whose root carries
a suppression, so a run measures what the mark seeds: the two declarations only the
root reaches are unreported, and dropping the mark reports the root and says three
symbols fall with it.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/selfcheckseed

go 1.27.1
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(kept()) }

func kept() string { return "k" }

//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- the root of a dead component
func root() string { return helper() }

func helper() string { return deeper() }

func deeper() string { return "d" }
